      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. The \"good faith\" angle is a solid foundation. \n\nBut I'm still struggling with the sheer \"noisiness\" of it. It's not just one big thing; it's a constant stream of these tiny, annoying, almost malicious-feeling disruptions. It's like they are operating in the shadows, avoiding any direct line of sight from our auditors. \n\nHow do we handle that \"shadowy\" aspect? How do we write something that gives us the right to look into those dark corners of their operation—to really expose those hidden, creeping issues—without it seeming like we're launching a full-scale investigation every time something small goes wrong?",
